# Backend logging

Use the shared logger for every new backend feature. Do not add `print()` or a second logging setup.

Salveris integration modules use `_logger = get_logger(__name__)`. Existing FastAPI modules may keep `logger`.

```python
from backend.logging_config import get_logger

_logger = get_logger(__name__)
_logger.info("Copilot search started (capability='%s')", capability)
```

| Level | When |
|-------|------|
| **INFO** | Lifecycle and significant start/complete (IDs, capability, counts). |
| **DEBUG** | Request shape, config comparison, match flags. Not method entry/exit. |
| **ERROR** | Failure before raise. Use `exc_info=True` when logging an exception. |

- Call `setup_logging()` only in process entrypoints (`backend/main.py` lifespan).
- Never log secrets, tokens, passwords, or `Authorization` values. For Salveris log IDs only plus `client_secret_configured=true|false`.
- Do not log full user questions. Use `question_len`.
- Do not log inside exception class definitions (`exceptions.py`).
- Avoid duplicating the same failure at every layer; log once at the handling boundary.
